  "note": "The application-key rule of SPEC 3.9 applies at the top level of a document only. A key containing a full stop on any other object this format defines is an unrecognised key (SPEC 6.2): diagnose it, skip the key, keep the object. The file puts one dotted key on every kind of object the format defines: folder, network, network arc, highlight, pass, network point, network area, plan, plan arc, track, segment, waypoint and top-level area, so a reader that forgets the key check on any one of them fails here. Every object survives, which counts pins. The top-level app.viatrail.datatypes in the same file is an application key and is not reported, so a reader that tests every object's keys for a full stop, and one that tests none, both fail this case. Information about one object belongs in its data array.",
